		<item>
		<title>Former TNA Knockouts Champion&#8217;s deal is expiring soon</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397415-former-tna-knockouts-champions-deal-is-expiring-soon/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397415-former-tna-knockouts-champions-deal-is-expiring-soon/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:57:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Impact News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[contract]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Xia Brookside]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397415</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Fightful Select is reporting that former TNA Knockouts Champion Xia Brookside’s contract is expiring soon. It was noted&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397415-former-tna-knockouts-champions-deal-is-expiring-soon/">Former TNA Knockouts Champion&#8217;s deal is expiring soon</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fightful Select is reporting that former TNA Knockouts Champion Xia Brookside’s contract is expiring soon. It was noted that both sides are currently negotiating a new deal. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The report adds they have heard TNA has communicated an offer to Brookside in hopes she will stay and that she is  under contract for a number of television tapings. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During the November 5 episode of IMPACT, Brookside was revealed as the newest member of The Righteous, attacking Harley Hudson. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brookside made her TNA debut at the 2024 Hard to Kill pay-per-view, as part of the Knockouts Ultimate X Match. She won the Knockouts Title from Léi Yǐng Lee in a no DQ match at Slammiversary. Brookside lost the title to Indie Hartwell at Bound For Glory last month. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Lee is <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-news/397323-former-tna-champion-reportedly-gone-from-company/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">reportedly gone from TNA</a> and speaking with <a href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/6TeKbm0zCWcPuzwPcepBOO" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Cultaholic Wrestling</a>, Trey Miguel revealed his current deal with TNA expires at the end of this year.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397415-former-tna-knockouts-champions-deal-is-expiring-soon/">Former TNA Knockouts Champion&#8217;s deal is expiring soon</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397415-former-tna-knockouts-champions-deal-is-expiring-soon/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>WWE SmackDown Results &#8211; 11/13/26 (John Cena to appear, Gunther battles Finn Bálor)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/397378-live-wwe-smackdown-results-november-13-2026/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/397378-live-wwe-smackdown-results-november-13-2026/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Mike Tedesco]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:08:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE Smackdown Results]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397378</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>WWE SmackDown ResultsNovember 13, 2026Fort Lauderdale, Florida (Amerant Bank Arena)Commentary: Michael Cole and Corey GravesResults by: Mike Tedesco&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/397378-live-wwe-smackdown-results-november-13-2026/">WWE SmackDown Results &#8211; 11/13/26 (John Cena to appear, Gunther battles Finn Bálor)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<figure class="wp-block-image is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="207" height="84" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/image-38.png" alt="" class="wp-image-354572" style="aspect-ratio:2.4642857142857144;width:207px;height:auto"/></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE SmackDown Results<br>November 13, 2026<br>Fort Lauderdale, Florida (Amerant Bank Arena)<br>Commentary: Michael Cole and Corey Graves<br>Results by: Mike Tedesco of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;Then. Now. Forever. Together.&#8221; The WWE video leads us into the show.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Video:</strong> <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396823-wwe-crown-jewel-results-11-7-26-mens-and-womens-crown-jewel-championships-and-more/">This past Saturday at WWE Crown Jewel</a>, Cody Rhodes punted Randy Orton in the head to win a Last Man Standing Match. World Heavyweight Champion Roman Reigns also showed respect to Undisputed WWE Champion Sami Zayn. Finally, Tiffany Stratton cashed in Money in the Bank on Chelsea Green, winning the WWE Women&#8217;s Championship.</p>



<h3 id="john-cena-reveals-the-next-invitee-to-the-john-cena-classic" class="wp-block-heading">John Cena reveals the next invitee to the John Cena Classic</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>John Cena</strong> comes out to a MASSIVE reception. Cena tells Stew they have to hit their time, then runs down to the ring. The John Cena Classic Championship is in the ring, and Cena spins the spinner belt. The crowd is going crazy for Cena. Cena says they don&#8217;t even need a warm-up. Cena holds up the spinner belt and says, &#8220;The Championship is here!&#8221; </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">On December 14, in a history-making event, live just a little up the road in Orlando, Florida, we will find out what happens to this title. The John Cena Classic is an evening of opportunity. On that night, a record-setting number of NXT Superstars will have their Raw debut matches against the best and the brightest that WWE has to offer, with all superstars having the opportunity to become a champ. The biggest opportunity of the night goes to their biggest superstar, the fans. They can use their voice to make sure it&#8217;s heard loud and clear.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">That&#8217;s December 14. How about we talk about right here and now? The time is now. It&#8217;s time to see who&#8217;s next. The next invitee to the John Cena Classic is&#8230; <strong>Charlotte Flair</strong>. The 14-time Women&#8217;s Champion heads to the ring. She gets on the apron and waits for an inexperienced stagehand to hold the ropes open for her. Flair finally gets in the ring and embraces Cena. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Flair says she&#8217;s her father&#8217;s daughter and tends to get emotional like him. She hopes she can make it through this. This is for Cena. For 10 years, she&#8217;s been trying to figure out how to get into a storyline to get in the ring and stand across from Cena. Flair has been trying to be a part of that magic. She&#8217;s dreamt it and manifested it to be in the ring with Cena because she thinks she&#8217;s that great, too. She knows her dad is at home in Tampa bawling with every TV on at that bar. Cena waves to Ric Flair. The reason why she&#8217;s here is that Cena wanted her to be part of his legacy. That means so much to her. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Flair doesn&#8217;t want to cry because her makeup is fabulous. Two years ago, after WrestleMania 41, she was backstage. Cena walked past her. She wasn&#8217;t wrestling. She was depressed and didn&#8217;t know if she wanted to be part of the company anymore or keep wrestling. Flair felt so lost. Cena looked her straight in the eyes and asked what happened in Chicago. Flair said she didn&#8217;t have an answer and &#8220;shit the bed.&#8221; It wasn&#8217;t her night. Cena looked at her and told her to stop trying to be perfect. Cena said, &#8220;Own who you are.&#8221; Since then, for the last two years, she&#8217;s gotten high-fives and been cheered. Flair isn&#8217;t saying she&#8217;s a fan favorite. She thanks Cena for helping her put on her big-girl pants, find her passion, and reinvent herself. Cena didn&#8217;t do it because she&#8217;s Ric Flair&#8217;s kid. Cena believed in her when she didn&#8217;t. Flair starts to cry. The crowd chants, &#8220;You deserve it.&#8221; Flair says when she doesn&#8217;t believe in herself, she&#8217;ll remember being in the John Cena Classic, being excellent in the John Cena Classic, and winning the John Cena Championship. Flair says she&#8217;s the greatest champion of all time. WOO!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cena says he&#8217;s going to go over his time, but he doesn&#8217;t care. When she started in the business, people thought she had an easy way in. Flair told him about the weight of carrying her father&#8217;s legacy, her brother, as well as rebuilding women&#8217;s wrestling and giving opportunities to today&#8217;s superstars. She never had it easy. She just made it look easy. There was a time when he said he needed to win 17 because he wanted to shake hands with whoever would win 18. Cena was always talking about her. Cena thanks her and embraces her before raising her arm.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">A good segment to kick off <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SmackDown?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SmackDown</a> with John Cena revealing Charlotte Flair as the next invitee to the Classic. Even though I don&#39;t totally love this concept, it clearly means a lot to the performers and the company. Flair did a nice job shooting from the hip here.</p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121415174326243773?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Locker Room Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>SmackDown General Manager Nick Aldis</strong> greets <strong>WWE Hall of Famer Rey Mysterio</strong>. Mysterio has an idea of someone who he could add to Team Mexico. <strong>Cody Rhodes</strong> walks in, greets Mysterio and Aldis. Mysterio says they have business, so he walks off. Aldis asks Rhodes about Crown Jewel and whether he&#8217;s in a good place, ready to leave that business behind. Rhodes says Crown Jewel will stick with him. Maybe he uses the Punt. Maybe not. Still, his attention is on Survivor Series. Aldis asks how recruiting is going for Team USA. Rhodes has some people in mind, as does CM Punk. Maybe they&#8217;ll add new members tonight or on Raw. After Survivor Series is behind them, Rhodes wants to revisit the No. 1 Contender conversation.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">WWE Tag Team Champions MFT make their entrance, accompanied by WWE Hall of Famer Haku. They&#8217;ll defend the titles against Bakusai next.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<h3 id="wwe-tag-team-championshipmft-tama-tonga-and-talla-tonga-w-haku-vs-bakusai-shinsuke-nakamura-and-kyoki" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>WWE Tag Team Championship</strong><br>MFT (Tama Tonga and Talla Tonga) w/ Haku vs. Bakusai (Shinsuke Nakamura and Kyoki)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Jason Ayers</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings, and Kyoki hits Tama Tonga with a pair of running crossbody blocks. Tama avoids one, but Kyoki comes right back with one. Tama quickly takes Kyoki down and tags Talla Tonga. Talla whips Kyoki hard into the corner before chopping him down. Talla stands him up and chops him down again. Tama tags in and chops Kyoki, but Kyoki begs for more. Kyoki hits the ropes and avoids a clothesline. Tama tries to block a running hurricanrana, but Kyoki takes him down. Kyoki attacks Talla, but he doesn&#8217;t knock him off the apron. As Talla tries to get into the ring, Kyoki kicks the rope into his groin. Tama puts Kyoki on the apron, but Kyoki knocks him back before kicking Talla in the face. Haku then breaks his Tongan Walking Stick on Kyoki&#8217;s knee.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Kyoki fights up from a rear chin lock applied by Tama. Tama sends Kyoki into the corner, but he runs into a boot. Kyoki blocks a kick, but Tama punches him. Kyoki soon fights back with a dragon screw.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Shinsuke Nakamura tags in and punches Tama before kicking him in the chest. Nakamura gives Tama some Good Vibrations. Tama reverses a whip to the opposite corner, but Nakamura sidesteps him. Nakamura kicks him in the neck before laying him across the top rope for a knee to the ribs. Nakamura knocks Talla off the apron and sizes Tama up for a Kinshasa. Nakamura catches him with a rebound wheel kick and goes to the corner. Tama avoids a Kinshasa and hits a Cutthroat Running Elbow. Tama goes for a double underhook move, but Nakamura counters with a back body drop before kneeing him in the head. Kyoki attacks Talla before he gets into the ring. Nakamura and Kyoki then give Talla a double clothesline over the top rope. Haku checks on Talla, and Kyoki baseball slides Haku into Talla! Kyoki then hits Talla with a missile dropkick off the apron!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In the ring, Nakamura hits Tama with a Kinshasa! 1&#8230; 2&#8230; <strong>The War Raiders</strong> run in and attack Nakamura.</p>



<h3 id="winners-by-disqualification-bakusai" class="wp-block-heading">Winners by Disqualification: Bakusai</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The War Raiders destroy everyone in the ring, finishing with a Ragnaroc on Nakamura.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">That was the definition of underwhelming with an equally horrible finish. What a waste of time. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SmackDown?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SmackDown</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121419210832372213?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cathy Kelley is backstage with <strong>Finn Bálor</strong>. Bálor says Gunther isn&#8217;t getting any of the ghosts of who Bálor was. It&#8217;s going to be him, and he&#8217;s confident.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Damian Priest is walking backstage.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Replay:</strong> Last week on SmackDown, Damian Priest viciously attacked Nathan Frazer and Axiom.</p>



<h3 id="axiom-vs-damian-priest" class="wp-block-heading">Axiom vs. Damian Priest</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Ryan Tran</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings, and Priest immediately rocks Axiom with a big boot. Priest hits him with a back elbow in the corner and throws him down. Priest sizes him up, but Axiom hits him with a pair of dropkicks to the knees. Priest grabs him, but Axiom fights him off. Priest quickly knees him in the midsection and charges, but Axiom sidesteps him. Axiom then dropkicks him out of the ring. Priest gets on the apron, but Axiom kicks him off. Axiom leaps to the top rope and hits a moonsault block to the floor! Axiom&#8217;s arm smashes off the commentary table, and he immediately grabs it. Axiom tries to fight through it and gets Priest in the ring. Priest quickly attacks him in the ring. Axiom snaps him off the ropes and hits a missile dropkick. Axiom&#8217;s arm appears to be fine as he sets up for a Golden Ratio. Priest avoids it and viciously forearms him in the jaw. Priest goes for a Razor&#8217;s Edge, but Axiom counters with a hurricanrana. Priest immediately turns him inside out with a clothesline, then hits the Razor&#8217;s Edge for the win.</p>



<h3 id="winner-by-pinfall-damian-priest" class="wp-block-heading">Winner by Pinfall: Damian Priest</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Nathan Frazer </strong>runs down to check on his partner, so Priest attacks him and hits South of Heaven.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">They keep trying with Damian Priest. After building him up in The Judgment Day, equal parts underwhelming performances and bad booking fumbled that opportunity. Since then, he&#39;s just been&#8230; there. They&#39;re trying again with him, but this was just&#8230; there. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SmackDown?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SmackDown</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121423237523603721?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>John Cena</strong> is walking backstage when <strong>Fatal Influence</strong> confronts him. Jacy Jayne says if he paid attention instead of just showing up whenever he wants, he&#8217;d know that leaving them out of the John Cena Classic is the biggest mistake he&#8217;s made since he tried to ruin wrestling. Cena agreed and invited them to join the John Cena Classic.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Video:</strong> The Bloodline will battle 946 in the Men&#8217;s WarGames match at Survivor Series on November 28.</p>



<h3 id="undisputed-wwe-champion-sami-zayn-addresses-wwe-crown-jewel" class="wp-block-heading">Undisputed WWE Champion Sami Zayn addresses WWE Crown Jewel</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Undisputed WWE Champion Sami Zayn</strong> heads to the ring alongside <strong>Johnny Gargano</strong> and <strong>Candice LeRae</strong>. At WWE Crown Jewel, World Heavyweight Champion Roman Reigns defeated him, but he showed respect to Zayn after the match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The crowd boos Zayn, and he tells them to bring it. Zayn tells Gargano they have some &#8220;bitch-ass haters&#8221; in the building tonight. That&#8217;s fine because he has to know&#8230; Zayn is cut off by a &#8220;You Suck&#8221; chant. Zayn says for the rest of them, he has to know how many are here to ride or die with the Last Real Good Guy? There&#8217;s a loud negative reaction, but some people are there to ride with him. Zayn says at Crown Jewel, a lot of things that were very wrong were made right. There was respect. Zayn wanted and needed the respect, and he got it. Zayn demanded it. He commanded it and took it. Zayn did something that no one in this industry has ever done. Zayn got Roman Reigns to acknowledge him. If the OTC, one of the all-time greats and the standard-bearer for this industry for the last ten years, could show him respect, that&#8217;s the bare minimum he wants from the people.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Kevin Owens</strong> heads to the ring! Owens warns Zayn that he&#8217;s not talking to Roman Reigns or Trick Williams. Owens is glad that Zayn got to right some wrongs because he&#8217;s done some of them as well. Last week, Owens punched CM Punk in the face with a chain to beat him in the middle of the ring without help from anyone, which is more than Punk could say about him. The other wrong that Owens wants to make right&#8230; Before he says this, he wants to be clear. Zayn talks about ride-or-die Sami Zayn fans; Owens has always said that Zayn is one of the best to ever do it, no matter what was going on with them. No matter how Zayn won the title, Owens believes he deserves every bit of it and the respect that comes with it. The people that try to diminish what he&#8217;s done, saying Zayn is a midcard guy who looks like a bum, aren&#8217;t half as good as Zayn on Zayn&#8217;s worst day. Owens believes that Zayn makes an excellent WWE Champion. From the bottom of his heart, Owens is proud of him.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Zayn is choked up and says that means the world to him. Owens says he&#8217;s not done. The wrong that he needs to make right is that 17 months of his career were taken from him. For 17 months, he sat at home and wondered if he&#8217;d ever get back into the ring. Without wrestling, Owens doesn&#8217;t know who he is. Owens wanted the people who saw him through the worst of times, his ride-or-die fans, to see him wrestle again. In Toronto on August 21, he got to do that. Owens also had an opportunity to become WWE Champion in front of them. It didn&#8217;t happen because of Zayn. Owens shoves Zayn. Zayn quickly holds Gargano back. Owens says he&#8217;s sorry to say that there&#8217;s only one way to right that wrong. Owens says he doesn&#8217;t want to take the title from Zayn&#8230; he NEEDS to take the title from him.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gargano steps in between them. Gargano says this was the worst year of his life. Gargano lost everything. The only man who stood by his side and showed him the respect he deserves was Sami Zayn. Zayn made him a promise and is working to get him a title match. Owens respects the Garganos, but Gargano lay on a crate for six months and got a title shot as soon as he stood up. He&#8217;s fine. Owens shoves him aside and gets in Zayn&#8217;s face, but Gargano attacks him from behind. Gargano holds Owens up, and LeRae slaps him in the face. Owens is struggling to get up. Zayn looks down at his friend and leaves the ring. Gargano attacaks OWens and kicks him in the face. Gargano goes for another kick, but Owens blocks it and hits a Stunner! Zayn isn&#8217;t happy. Owens grabs a microphone and says Zayn&#8217;s title reign is on borrowed time, and he will end it. Owens then sends Gargano over the top rope.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">A very good segment with Sami Zayn and Kevin Owens. Sounds like a great title match at <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SurvivorSeries?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SurvivorSeries</a>. I liked the stuff with Owens and Johnny Gargano as well. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SmackDown?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SmackDown</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121428164152848402?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>CM Punk </strong>is watching this segment when <strong>Cody Rhodes</strong> approaches him. Punk says he still hasn&#8217;t gotten his rematch. <strong>Rey Mysterio </strong>walks up and introduces <strong>AAA World Cruiserweight Champion Rey Fénix</strong> as the next member of Team Mexico. Punk says they&#8217;ve got some recruiting to do. Rhodes says he has a plan, but Punk hands him a slip of paper with some suggestions. Rhodes says he loves suggestions.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">WWE Women&#8217;s United States Champion Jacy Jayne makes her way to the ring. She battles Charlotte Flair next.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<h3 id="non-title-matchwwe-womens-united-states-champion-jacy-jayne-vs-charlotte-flair" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Non-Title Match</strong><br>WWE Women&#8217;s United States Champion Jacy Jayne vs. Charlotte Flair</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Daphne LaShaunn</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They lock up, and Jayne strikes her before bouncing her off the top turnbuckle. Flair reverses a whip, but Jayne hits her with a hurricanrana. Jayne mocks the Flair Strut and goes for a running back elbow, but Flair catches her and hits a back suplex. Flair then does the famous strut. Flair grapevines Jayne&#8217;s head and rolls her around the mat. Jayne tries to fight back, but Flair boots her back. Flair goes to the top rope and hits a diving crossbody block for a two-count. Jayne soon knocks Flair back, but Flair big boots her to the floor. Flair goes to the apron and hits a cannonball.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Lainey Reid</strong> and <strong>Fallon Henley</strong> come down and distract Flair, allowing Jayne to kick her in the face. <strong>Alexa Bliss</strong> and <strong>Tatum Paxley</strong> come down to even the odds.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Flair lifts Jayne and hits a fallaway slam before doing a kip up. Jayne quickly kicks her back, but Flair hits her third big boot of the match for a two-count. Flair pulls Jayne up and goes for a back suplex, but Jayne flips through and hits a neckbreaker. Jayne talks trash to Bliss and Paxley at ringside before covering Flair for a two-count. Jayne charges, but Flair hits a backbreaker before slinging her face into the top turnbuckle. Flair steps on Jayne and goes to the top rope for a moonsault. 1&#8230; 2&#8230; Jayne kicks out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They go back and forth with pinning attempts before Flair goes for a Figure Four Leglock. Jayne counters with an inside cradle for a two-count. Flair hits a backslide, but Jayne rolls through and knees her in the face for a near fall. Jayne is furious. Jayne sizes Flair up for a Rolling Encore, but Flair ducks and hits a Spear. Flair goes to the top rope, but Reid gets on the apron. Flair kicks her down before hitting Henley. Paxley takes Henley out, and Bliss takes care of Reid. <strong>WWE Women&#8217;s Tag Team Champions B-Fab and Michin</strong> run down and attack. <strong>Bayley</strong> comes down with a kendo stick. <strong>Jade Cargill</strong> then appears and big boots Bayley. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Stephanie Vaquer</strong> then returns and takes out Michin. Vaquer breaks the kendo stick off Michin&#8217;s back. In the ring, Flair hits Jayne with a Natural Selection for the win.</p>



<h3 id="winner-by-pinfall-charlotte-flair" class="wp-block-heading">Winner by Pinfall: Charlotte Flair</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Flair and the other faces get in the ring and shout, &#8220;WarGames!&#8221;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">The men&#39;s WarGames match has been built naturally and makes sense. Then there&#39;s this, seemingly thrown together just so the women can have one, too. Why does every specialty match need a men&#39;s and women&#39;s version? If the story doesn&#39;t warrant it, don&#39;t force it. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SmackDown?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SmackDown</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121432349371982283?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Charlotte Flair, Alexa Bliss, Tatum Paxley, Bayley, and Stephanie Vaquer are walking backstage when Cathy Kelley stops them. Vaquer said she couldn&#8217;t say no when Flair called her.</p>



<h3 id="wwe-womens-champion-tiffany-stratton-addresses-her-victory" class="wp-block-heading">WWE Women&#8217;s Champion Tiffany Stratton addresses her victory</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE Women&#8217;s Champion Tiffany Stratton</strong> makes her way to the ring as replays show her cashing in Money in the Bank on Chelsea Green at WWE Crown Jewel. Stratton says some people need a boyfriend or a General Manager to feel bad for them. All Stratton needs is a briefcase. Stratton dedicates this victory to her former BFF, Chelsea Green.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Chelsea Green</strong> heads to the ring and says it&#8217;s noted that she&#8217;s Stratton&#8217;s ex-BFF. A &#8220;Chelsea&#8221; chant picks up. Green says they were clearly never friends. Stratton was faking because she stood beside her as she told her how much Crown Jewel meant to her. Green told her how much Crown Jewel could change the trajectory of her career. Why her? Green&#8217;s been thinking about it. Was it the ring or the title? No, it was Stratton wanting to steal Green&#8217;s moment. Stratton did it, but when Green lays her head on her pillow, she&#8217;ll sleep soundly after going down in the history books as the Crown Jewel Champion. Stratton is a thief, and Green wants her ring back.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Stratton says Green stole her moment at SummerSlam. Green has gotten too comfortable thinking she&#8217;s on Stratton&#8217;s level. There&#8217;s Tiffany Stratton, everyone else, and then Chelsea Green. Stratton takes off the Crown Jewel ring and says, &#8220;Enjoy the rest of your career in catering, bitch.&#8221; Green attacks Stratton and picks up the ring, but Stratton attacks her from behind. Stratton puts the ring on and punches Green in the face.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Just a segment with Chelsea Green and Tiffany Stratton. This show is so blah. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SmackDown?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SmackDown</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121435020959383989?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Coming up next, Gunther battles Finn Bálor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A dejected <strong>Chelsea Green</strong> is walking backstage when <strong>Paige</strong> checks on her. <strong>Blake Monroe</strong> walks up and makes fun of Green before saying Monroe&#8217;s best years are ahead of her.</p>



<h3 id="the-ring-general-gunther-vs-finn-balor" class="wp-block-heading">&#8220;The Ring General&#8221; Gunther vs. Finn Bálor</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Charles Robinson</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gunther attacks Bálor with a kick and uppercuts him several times. Gunther sends him into the ropes and hits a stiff back elbow. Gunther punches away at Bálor and stomps him. Gunther stands Bálor up and immediately chops him down. Gunther talks trash to the crowd and knees Bálor in the midsection twice. Gunther goes for a Powerbomb. Bálor tries to counter with a back body drop, but Gunther counters into a roll-up attempt. Bálor rolls through and dropkicks him before getting him out of the ring. Bálor then wipes Gunther out with a somersault plancha.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Gunther has Bálor on the top rope. Gunther goes for a superplex, but Bálor fights it. Bálor punches Gunther, but Gunther rocks him with some headbutts. Bálor drops him to the canvas with a snap kick. Bálor heads to the top rope, but Gunther greets him with a chop. Gunther pulls him down to the canvas and digs his boot into his face. Gunther scoops him up, but Bálor slides off and kicks at his legs. Gunther immediately responds with a scoop slam.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After taking a few moments, Gunther grabs Bálor and elbows him in the bridge of his nose. Gunther sends Bálor into the ropes, but he lowers his head and eats a kick. Gunther reverses a whip, but Bálor hits a head-scissor into a Russian leg sweep. They slowly get up, and Bálor attacks Gunther. Gunther reverses a whip, but Bálor takes him down with a running back elbow. Bálor chops Gunther and hits a falling elbow drop for a two-count. Bálor kicks at Gunther’s chest, but Gunther blocks one and goes for a Powerbomb. Bálor fights it and pulls Gunther over the top rope with a hurricanrana. Bálor sizes him up from the apron, but Gunther blocks a kick and sweeps his feet out from under him. Gunther then hits Bálor with a back suplex on the barricade!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the evening&#8217;s final break, Gunther stands over Bálor. Gunther absolutely smokes Bálor’s chest with a massive chop. Bálor pops up and shoves Gunther, but Gunther shoves him down. Gunther chops Bálor and laughs at him. Bálor is gasping for air. Bálor gets to his feet and hits Bálor with a strike combo. Bálor avoids a Sleeper Hold and goes for an O’Connor Roll, but Gunther attempts a Sleeper Hold. Bálor rolls back and picks up a two-count. Bálor fires back with a Sling Blade. Bálor goes for a Woo Dropkick, but Gunther hooks him for a Sleeper Hold. Bálor hits a Woo Dropkick, but Gunther fights it off and soon viciously hits him with a lariat for a near fall!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Both men are down. Gunther says he told Bálor for weeks that it’s time to move on. Bálor needs to stop embarrassing himself any further. Gunther grabs Bálor and turns him over. Gunther slowly saunters to the apron and signals for a diving splash. Gunther goes to the top rope for a splash, but Bálor moves. Bálor hits a Woo Dropkick before heading to the top rope. Bálor goes for a Coup de Grâce, but Gunther moves. Gunther shoves Bálor into the referee and chops him in the back. Gunther then kicks Bálor in the groin and hits a Powerbomb for the win.</p>



<h3 id="winner-by-pinfall-the-ring-general-gunther" class="wp-block-heading">Winner by Pinfall: “The Ring General” Gunther</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gunther celebrates over Bálor as the show comes to an end.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">A really good match with Gunther and Finn Bálor. Hopefully, rumors of Gunther&#39;s demise have been greatly exaggerated. The company gives a choice not to go into a war zone, and he took it. Why would he be punished for it? <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SmackDown?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SmackDown</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121441715923865672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">This was a good match to end a show that had some major lulls. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SmackDown?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SmackDown</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121441827001639010?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 id="quick-match-results" class="wp-block-heading">Quick Match Results</h3>



<p class="cnvs-block-core-paragraph-1794621394476 wp-block-paragraph">&#8212; Bakusai (Shinsuke Nakamura and Kyoki) def. The MFTs (Tama Tonga and Talla Tonga) (c&#8217;s) via DQ in a WWE Tag Team Championship match<br>&#8212; Damian Priest def. Axiom<br>&#8212; Charlotte Flair def. WWE Women&#8217;s United States Champion Jacy Jayne in a Non-Title Match<br>&#8212; &#8220;The Ring General&#8221; Gunther def. Finn Bálor</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Email –&nbsp;<a href="mailto:mike@wrestleview.com">mike@wrestleview.com</a><br>X –&nbsp;<a href="https://x.com/MikeTedescoWV">@MikeTedescoWV</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Check out our retro recaps of WWF Raw and WCW Nitro, 30 years after their original airings, every Thursday on Wrestleview!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/retro/397331-wwf-raw-results-november-11-1996-fort-wayne/">Check out this week&#8217;s Raw from 30 years ago!</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thanks for reading!</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/397378-live-wwe-smackdown-results-november-13-2026/">WWE SmackDown Results &#8211; 11/13/26 (John Cena to appear, Gunther battles Finn Bálor)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/397378-live-wwe-smackdown-results-november-13-2026/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
